APX.rs = {"country":{"name":"Serbia","tagline":"Prokupac and Tamjanika, Fruška Gora's monastery slopes and Bermet, and the stone cellar towns of Negotin.","classification":"Serbia's wine law defines wines with geographical origin in three tiers: *kontrolisano poreklo* (KP, controlled origin), *kontrolisano poreklo i kvalitet* (KPK, controlled origin and quality) and *kontrolisano poreklo i garantovan kvalitet* (KPGK, controlled origin and guaranteed quality). These terms are registered as traditional terms under Serbia's agreements with the EU and UK. The 2015 zoning sets three wine-growing units, 22 regions (*rejoni*) and 77 districts (*vinogorja*). Under the UK-Serbia Partnership, Trade and Cooperation Agreement (2021) 81 Serbian wine names are protected as PGIs. Other traditional terms include *kasna berba* (late harvest), *suvarak* (dried-grape wine), *arhivsko vino* (archive wine) and *mlado vino* (young wine)."},"regions":[{"name":"Vojvodina","slug":"vojvodina","tagline":"Fruška Gora's monasteries, Sremski Karlovci's Bermet and the Banat hills of Vršac.","ids":["rs-banat","rs-banat-tisa","rs-bela-crkva","rs-deliblato-sands","rs-fruska-gora","rs-horgos","rs-northern-banat","rs-palic","rs-southern-banat","rs-srem","rs-subotica-horgos-sands","rs-vrsac"]},{"name":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","slug":"umadija-and-central-serbia","tagline":"The rolling heart of Serbia: Oplenac's royal winery, Župa's Prokupac and the Morava valleys.","ids":["rs-belgrade","rs-branicevo","rs-cer","rs-dobric","rs-dubona","rs-grocka","rs-jagodina","rs-jelica","rs-kosmaj","rs-kragujevac","rs-krnjevo","rs-krusevac","rs-levac","rs-ljubic","rs-mlava","rs-oplenac","rs-oreovica","rs-paracin","rs-podgorina","rs-rasina","rs-raca","rs-resava","rs-smederevo","rs-tamnava","rs-temnic","rs-trstenik","rs-vencac","rs-zapadna-morava","rs-cacak","rs-sumadija-velika-morava","rs-zupa"]},{"name":"Eastern Serbia","slug":"eastern-serbia","tagline":"The Timok and Negotin Krajina: stone cellar villages, Bagrina and black Tamjanika near the Danube.","ids":["rs-boljevac","rs-bor","rs-brza-palanka","rs-dzervin","rs-kljuc","rs-knjazevac","rs-krajina","rs-mihajlovac","rs-negotin","rs-rajac","rs-sokobanja","rs-timok","rs-vrbica","rs-zajecar"]},{"name":"Southern Serbia","slug":"southern-serbia","tagline":"Toplica and Niš: Prokupac's homeland in the warm south.","ids":["rs-aleksinac","rs-babicka-gora","rs-babusnica","rs-bela-palanka","rs-bustranje","rs-jovac","rs-kutina","rs-leskovac","rs-matejevac","rs-nis","rs-nisava","rs-nisava-juzna-morava","rs-pirot","rs-prokuplje","rs-pusta-reka","rs-razanj","rs-sicevo","rs-surdulica","rs-toplica","rs-vinarce","rs-vlasotince","rs-vranje","rs-vrtogos","rs-zitkovac"]}],"items":{"rs-aleksinac":{"name":"Aleksinac","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Aleksinac lies on the Južna Morava north of Niš; its hills grow Prokupac and Smederevka. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-babicka-gora":{"name":"Babička gora","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Babička gora is a mountain near Leskovac in southern Serbia with vineyards on its lower slopes. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-babusnica":{"name":"Babušnica","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Babušnica lies in the Lužnica valley near Pirot in south-eastern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-banat":{"name":"Banat","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Riesling, Kreaca, Smederevka, Frankovka","summary":"Banat is the broad PGI for the Serbian part of the historic Banat region east of the Tisa, divided further into Southern Banat, Northern Banat and Banat-Tisa. It is mostly flat, with vineyards concentrated around Vršac and Bela Crkva.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-banat-tisa":{"name":"Banat-Tisa","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Banat-Tisa covers the Banat plain along the Tisa river in northern Vojvodina. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-bela-crkva":{"name":"Bela Crkva","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Bela Crkva, a lake town in the southern Banat near the Romanian border, has vineyards on the last hills of the Carpathian foreland. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-bela-palanka":{"name":"Bela Palanka","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Bela Palanka lies on the Nišava between Niš and Pirot in south-eastern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-belgrade":{"name":"Belgrade","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Smederevka, Graševina, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"The Belgrade PGI covers vineyards within the capital's territory, including Grocka on the Danube and the Kosmaj and Dubona hills to the south. Grocka's Danube slopes were among the capital's main vineyards before the city spread.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-boljevac":{"name":"Boljevac","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Boljevac lies at the foot of Rtanj mountain in eastern Serbia's Crna Reka valley. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-bor":{"name":"Bor","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Bor, a copper-mining town in eastern Serbia, has small vineyards in the surrounding Timok hills. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-branicevo":{"name":"Braničevo","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Braničevo covers the hills around Požarevac east of Belgrade, near the Danube and the Mlava. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-brza-palanka":{"name":"Brza Palanka","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Brza Palanka is a Danube village below the Iron Gates in the Negotin Krajina. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-bustranje":{"name":"Buštranje","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Buštranje is a village in the Preševo valley in the far south of Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-cacak":{"name":"Čačak","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Čačak, in the West Morava valley, is the centre of a hilly district of vineyards and plum orchards. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-cer":{"name":"Cer","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Cer is the mountain near Šabac in western Serbia, site of a 1914 Serbian victory, with vineyards on its slopes. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-deliblato-sands":{"name":"Deliblato Sands","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Smederevka, Kreaca, Frankovka","summary":"Deliblato Sands, Europe's largest continental sand area, in the southern Banat, has vineyards on its edges planted, like Hungary's Kunság, on phylloxera-proof sand. The dunes, now a nature reserve, were stabilised with forest in the 19th century, and the vineyards on their fringes make light, fresh whites.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-dobric":{"name":"Dobrić","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Dobrić is a village near Šabac in the Mačva region of western Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-dubona":{"name":"Dubona","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Dubona is a village in Mladenovac, south of Belgrade, on the edge of Šumadija. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-dzervin":{"name":"Džervin","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Džervin is the hill above Knjaževac on the upper Timok where the town's oldest vineyards grew; the name also lives on in the Džervin cellar, which grew out of the Knjaževac wine cooperative of 1927. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-fruska-gora":{"name":"Fruška Gora","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Riesling, Sremska Zelenika, Morava, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Frankovka, Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Fruška Gora is a forested ridge on the right bank of the Danube opposite Novi Sad, rising to 539 m, with vineyards on its loess and marl slopes. Probus is credited with planting it in the 3rd century, and from the 16th century its sixteen Orthodox monasteries kept the vine alive. Sremski Karlovci, the old metropolitan seat at its eastern foot, is the wine capital and the home of Bermet. Today about 60 wineries work the ridge, making Graševina, Riesling, Sremska Zelenika, Morava, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc and reds from Frankovka, Merlot and Cabernet. Leading names include Kovačević, Erdevik (whose cellar dates to 1826), Trivanović, Probus, Šijački and Živanović.","terroir":"Loess and marl over Paleozoic schist; south-facing slopes 150 to 400 m; continental climate tempered by the Danube.","producers":["Kovačević","Erdevik","Trivanović","Probus","Živanović","Šijački","Deurić","Vinum"],"contains":["Sremski Karlovci"],"rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-grocka":{"name":"Grocka","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Grocka is a Danube-side municipality of Belgrade, historically known for its vineyards and orchards. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-horgos":{"name":"Horgoš","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Horgoš is a village on the Hungarian border north of Kanjiža, on the edge of the northern sands. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-jagodina":{"name":"Jagodina","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Jagodina lies on the Velika Morava in central Serbia; its PGI covers the hills of the Pomoravlje district. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-jelica":{"name":"Jelica","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Jelica is a mountain near Čačak in western Serbia, with vineyards on its southern slopes. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-jovac":{"name":"Jovac","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Jovac is a village near Vladičin Han in the Južna Morava valley in southern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-kljuc":{"name":"Ključ","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Ključ is the Danube-side district around Kladovo in the Negotin Krajina. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-knjazevac":{"name":"Knjaževac","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Knjaževac, on the upper Timok, has a revived wine scene led by family wineries. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-kosmaj":{"name":"Kosmaj","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Kosmaj is a wooded mountain south of Belgrade whose slopes hold vineyards around Sopot. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-kragujevac":{"name":"Kragujevac","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Kragujevac, Serbia's first modern capital (1818 to 1841), is the centre of Šumadija. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-krajina":{"name":"Krajina","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Gamay, Tamjanika, Bagrina","summary":"Krajina is the PGI for the wider Negotin Krajina along the Danube and Timok, framing Negotin, Rajac, Mihajlovac and Ključ. The Danube's Iron Gates gorge moderates the climate, and the area's stone cellar villages are unique in the Balkans.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-krnjevo":{"name":"Krnjevo","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Krnjevo is a village near Velika Plana on the Velika Morava. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-krusevac":{"name":"Kruševac","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika, Smederevka, Vranac","summary":"Kruševac, Prince Lazar's medieval capital, is home to the Rubin company, once Yugoslavia's largest brandy and wine producer. The PGI covers the surrounding Rasina hills, which share the warm, sheltered conditions of neighbouring Župa and grow Prokupac and Tamjanika.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-kutina":{"name":"Kutina","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Kutina is a district near Niška Banja, east of Niš. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-leskovac":{"name":"Leskovac","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Leskovac, in the Južna Morava valley, is a southern Serbian centre of Prokupac. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-levac":{"name":"Levač","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Levač is a hilly district west of the Velika Morava near Rekovac, home to Lastar (founded 2013) and other new wineries reviving Prokupac and Tamjanika on the district's rolling clay hills.","producers":["Lastar"],"rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-ljubic":{"name":"Ljubić","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Ljubić is the hill district of Čačak in western Serbia, site of an 1815 battle of the Second Serbian Uprising. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-matejevac":{"name":"Matejevac","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Matejevac, on the hills just north-east of Niš, is the city's historic vineyard quarter. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-mihajlovac":{"name":"Mihajlovac","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Mihajlovac is a Danube village in the Negotin Krajina north of Negotin. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-mlava":{"name":"Mlava","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Mlava covers the Mlava river valley around Požarevac and Petrovac; Virtus winery is based here. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-negotin":{"name":"Negotin","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Gamay, Crna Tamjanika, Bagrina, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Negotin, in the Krajina by the Danube's Iron Gates near the Bulgarian and Romanian borders, is famous for its stone cellar villages (*pivnice*) at Rajac, Rogljevo and Štubik, on Serbia's UNESCO Tentative List since 2010. Its warm hills grow Prokupac, black Tamjanika, Gamay, Bagrina and Bordeaux varieties. During France's phylloxera crisis Negotin wine was sold to French merchants.","producers":["Matalj","Raj","Rajačke pivnice"],"contains":["Rajac pivnice","Rogljevo pivnice"],"rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-nis":{"name":"Niš","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika, Smederevka","summary":"Niš, Roman Naissus and birthplace of Constantine the Great, has vineyards on the surrounding hills; Matejevac's slopes above the city are its best-known district, with a cellar row and a tradition of Prokupac and Tamjanika going back centuries.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-nisava":{"name":"Nišava","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Nišava is the PGI for the Nišava river valley between Pirot and Niš. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-nisava-juzna-morava":{"name":"Nišava-Južna Morava","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Nišava-Južna Morava is the broad PGI for south-eastern Serbia's river valleys. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-northern-banat":{"name":"Northern Banat","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Northern Banat covers the flat north-east of Vojvodina around Kikinda. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-oplenac":{"name":"Oplenac","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Traminer, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Tamjanika, Pinot Noir, Gamay, Prokupac, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Oplenac is the hill above Topola where King Peter I built the white marble Church of St George and the Karađorđević mausoleum. His son, King Alexander I, built the King's Winery at its foot in 1931 on the French model, with two underground floors held at 8 °C and 99 oak casks of 2,000 litres, and planted over 50 ha with Traminer, Chardonnay, Gamay and Pinot Noir. The vineyards were neglected after 1945 and replanted in the 2000s; the first new harvest was in 2006. Aleksandrović's Trijumf, a nearby estate wine, follows a royal blend recipe from 1932.","producers":["Kraljevski podrumi (King's Winery)","Aleksandrović"],"rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-oreovica":{"name":"Oreovica","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Oreovica is a village near Požarevac in the Braničevo district. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-palic":{"name":"Palić","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Riesling, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Muscat, Kadarka, Frankovka, Cabernet Franc","summary":"Palić, a resort lake near Subotica on the Hungarian border, grows vines on wind-blown sands that once kept phylloxera at bay. Zvonko Bogdan, the famous tamburica singer, built a 62 ha estate here; Vinarija Čoka and Dibonis are other producers.","producers":["Zvonko Bogdan","Dibonis","Čoka"],"rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-paracin":{"name":"Paraćin","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Paraćin lies on the Velika Morava in central Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-pirot":{"name":"Pirot","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Pirot, near the Bulgarian border, is better known for kilims and cheese, but has small vineyards in the Nišava valley. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-podgorina":{"name":"Podgorina","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Podgorina is a hilly district near Valjevo in western Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-prokuplje":{"name":"Prokuplje","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika","summary":"Prokuplje, the medieval town that gave Prokupac its name, has its own PGI for the hills around the town in the Toplica valley. The town's name and the grape's are the same root, and Prokupac is still the dominant variety.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-pusta-reka":{"name":"Pusta reka","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Pusta reka is a valley near Bojnik in the Jablanica district of southern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-raca":{"name":"Rača","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Rača is a municipality in eastern Šumadija near Kragujevac. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-rajac":{"name":"Rajac","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Gamay, Tamjanika, Bagrina","summary":"Rajac is a village in the Negotin Krajina whose cellar settlement, about 2 km west on the Beli Breg hill, is the finest of the region's pivnice: a cluster of stone cellars with arched portals along winding lanes next to a 19th-century cemetery. The PGI covers its vineyards.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-rasina":{"name":"Rasina","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Rasina is the broad PGI for the Rasina district around Kruševac, including Župa. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-razanj":{"name":"Ražanj","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Ražanj is a small municipality between Paraćin and Aleksinac. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-resava":{"name":"Resava","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Resava is the valley around Despotovac in central Serbia, near the 15th-century Manasija monastery. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-sicevo":{"name":"Sićevo","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Sićevo lies at the mouth of the Sićevo gorge of the Nišava east of Niš, a historic vineyard area. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-smederevo":{"name":"Smederevo","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Smederevo, the 15th-century Danube fortress capital of the Serbian Despotate, gave its name to the Smederevka grape. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-sokobanja":{"name":"Sokobanja","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Sokobanja is a spa town in eastern Serbia with small hillside vineyards. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-southern-banat":{"name":"Southern Banat","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Riesling, Kreaca, Frankovka, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Southern Banat covers the Vršac hills, Bela Crkva and the Deliblato sands down to the Danube; it is the most important part of the Serbian Banat for wine. Riesling, Kreaca and Frankovka from the Vršac hills are its best-known wines.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-srem":{"name":"Srem","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Riesling, Chardonnay, Frankovka, Merlot","summary":"Srem is the broader PGI for the Syrmia region between the Danube and the Sava, including Fruška Gora and its plains. It is used for blends and for wines from the lower slopes.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-subotica-horgos-sands":{"name":"Subotica-Horgoš Sands","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Kadarka, Graševina, Riesling, Kövidinka","summary":"The Subotica-Horgoš sands in the far north are a continuation of Hungary's Great Plain sand vineyards, planted on dunes that phylloxera could not penetrate. Light whites and Kadarka are traditional.","rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-sumadija-velika-morava":{"name":"Šumadija-Velika Morava","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Smederevka, Tamjanika, Prokupac, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Šumadija-Velika Morava is the broad PGI for the central Serbian heartland between the Sava, Danube and Velika Morava, around Topola, Kragujevac, Aranđelovac, Smederevo and Jagodina. It is the catch-all name for wines blended across the rolling, mixed-farming hills of the Serbian heartland.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-surdulica":{"name":"Surdulica","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Surdulica lies in the hills of the far south near the Vlasina plateau. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-tamnava":{"name":"Tamnava","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Tamnava is a district in the Kolubara basin of western Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-temnic":{"name":"Temnić","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Temnić is the area around Varvarin at the confluence of the West and South Morava. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-timok":{"name":"Timok","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Gamay, Tamjanika, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Timok is the broad PGI for the Timok river valley in eastern Serbia, from Knjaževac through Zaječar to Negotin. Small family wineries around Knjaževac and Zaječar are reviving the area, and the late-Roman palace of Felix Romuliana near Zaječar is a reminder of the valley's ancient importance.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-toplica":{"name":"Toplica","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika, Smederevka, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Toplica, the valley of the Toplica river around Prokuplje, gave its name to Prokupac and remains the grape's heartland. Warm summers give fuller, spicier Prokupac than in the north, and growers here are leading the effort to make the grape a serious varietal wine rather than a blending component.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-trstenik":{"name":"Trstenik","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Trstenik on the West Morava is near the medieval Ljubostinja monastery, with vineyards on both sides of the valley. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-vencac":{"name":"Venčac","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Venčac is a marble-quarry mountain near Aranđelovac in Šumadija with vineyards on its slopes. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-vinarce":{"name":"Vinarce","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Vinarce, whose name comes from the word for wine, is a village near Leskovac in southern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-vlasotince":{"name":"Vlasotince","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Vlasotince on the Vlasina river near Leskovac is an old Prokupac-growing town of southern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-vranje":{"name":"Vranje","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Vranac, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Tamjanika","summary":"Vranje, in the far south near North Macedonia, is a warm, hilly PGI where Aleksić and other wineries make Prokupac, Vranac and international reds. Aleksić, one of Serbia's most awarded wineries, produces about 450,000 litres a year.","producers":["Aleksić"],"rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-vrbica":{"name":"Vrbica","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Vrbica is a village near Zaječar in the Timok valley of eastern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-vrsac":{"name":"Vršac","cat":"PGI","region":"Vojvodina","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Graševina, Banat Riesling, Rhine Riesling, Kreaca, Chardonnay, Smederevka, Frankovka","summary":"Vršac lies at the foot of the Vršac hills, the only real elevation of the Serbian Banat, near the Romanian border. In the 19th century its vineyards spread over about 10,000 ha; today about 2,000 ha remain, much of it once worked by the state company Vršački vinogradi, whose 1968 'New Cellar' with a capacity of about 20 million litres was one of the largest in Europe. Riesling (Italian, Banat and Rhine), Kreaca, Chardonnay and Frankovka grow on loess and schist; Gudurica's estates (Vinarija Selecta, Kreačić) and Vršac's family wineries are reviving quality.","producers":["Vršački vinogradi","Selecta","Nedin","Kreačić"],"rslug":"vojvodina"},"rs-vrtogos":{"name":"Vrtogoš","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Vrtogoš is a village near Vranje in southern Serbia. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-zajecar":{"name":"Zaječar","cat":"PGI","region":"Eastern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Zaječar is the main town of the Timok valley, near the late-Roman imperial palace of Felix Romuliana (Gamzigrad), a UNESCO site. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"eastern-serbia"},"rs-zapadna-morava":{"name":"Zapadna Morava","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Zapadna Morava is the broad PGI for the West Morava valley from Čačak to Kruševac, including Župa and Trstenik. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"},"rs-zitkovac":{"name":"Žitkovac","cat":"PGI","region":"Southern Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"Žitkovac is a village near Aleksinac on the Južna Morava. Like most of Serbia's 81 wine geographical indications, it is protected under the 2021 UK-Serbia trade agreement and corresponds to a district of the national zoning; few producers use the name on labels so far.","rslug":"southern-serbia"},"rs-zupa":{"name":"Župa","cat":"PGI","region":"Šumadija and Central Serbia","created":"PGI (UK register 2021)","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Prokupac, Tamjanika, Smederevka, Graševina, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Župa is a warm, sheltered valley around Aleksandrovac in the Rasina district, ringed by the Kopaonik, Goč and Jastrebac mountains, and Serbia's self-styled wine capital. Monastic charters record its vineyards in the Nemanjić era, and legend says Prince Lazar's army took communion with Župa wine before the 1389 Battle of Kosovo. Prokupac and Tamjanika are the stars. Aleksandrovac's Župska berba harvest festival has run every September since 1963, and the town has a museum of viticulture.","producers":["Budimir","Ivanović","Spasić","Rubin (Kruševac)"],"rslug":"umadija-and-central-serbia"}}};
